  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nA weak upper-level ridge is over North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. This will allow temperatures to warm up today. \nDue to a strong surface pressure gradient and strong low-level winds \nit will be windy across North-central Montana this afternoon through \nearly Saturday morning with the strongest winds along the Rocky \nMountain Front and plains west of I-15. This afternoon it will be \nmostly dry. On Saturday the upper-level ridge strengthens and the \nstrong winds aloft move higher into the atmosphere. This results in \nwarm and dry weather for the area with strong winds ending by mid-\nmorning on Saturday.\n\nOn Sunday the upper-level ridge breaks down. This combined with \nstrong low-level and mid-level winds will bring another day of windy \nconditions to North-central Montana. The strongest winds will be \nalong the Rocky Mountain Front with an extension of strongest winds \nfrom favorable mountain wave effects downrange over the northern \nplains west of I-15. On Sunday it will be dry. On Monday an upper-\nlevel ridge moves back over North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana. This will continue the warm and dry conditions for the \narea. Tuesday through Thursday the upper-level ridge remains over \nNorth-central Montana. This will keep warm and dry weather for the \narea Tuesday through Thursday. Tuesday through Thursday it will also \nbe breezy across North-central Montana. -IG/RA\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nEarly Saturday morning there is a 30 - 60% chance for wind gusts of \n70 mph or greater along the Rocky Mountain Front. For winds along \nthe plains west of I-15 this afternoon into Sunday morning there is \na 30 - 60% chance for wind gusts of 55 mph along the plains west of \nI-15. As a result a High Wind Warning was issued for those areas \nthrough 9 am Saturday. Across most of the rest of North-central \nMontana there is a 30 - 60% chance for wind gusts of 55 mph or \ngreater.\n\nOn Sunday along the Hi-line east of I-15 and in the lower-elevations \nof Cascade County there is a 30 - 70% chance for wind gusts of 55 \nmph or greater. On Sunday along the Rocky Mountain Front there is a \n40 - 70% chance for wind gusts of 80 mph or greater. On Sunday \nacross the plains west of I-15 there is a 50 - 90% chance for wind \ngusts of 70 mph or greater. As a result during the day on Sunday the \nHigh Wind Watch for Glacier County, Western Toole County, Pondera \nCounty, and the Rocky Mountain Front of Teton and Lewis and Clark Co \nhas been upgraded to a High Wind Warning. Eastern Toole, Liberty, \nHill, and Cascade County remain in a High Wind Watch. -IG/RA",
